// 23_multi_row.mty — multi row-variable fn signatures (v0.17 RFC-008
// typeck extension + v0.18 parser surface).
//
// Build:
//   mty fmt examples/23_multi_row.mty
//   mty check examples/23_multi_row.mty
//
// As of v0.17 the typeck layer can represent and validate fn
// signatures with multiple row variables — every fn-typed parameter
// gets its own RowSubst-allocated fresh row at each call site, and
// the caller's inferred effect set is the UNION of all closure
// rows. The HIR `HirEffectRow::Open` field is now `Vec<HirRowVar>`,
// the `UserRowPolyIndex` carries per-fn `UserRowPolyMeta`
// (`row_vars` + `fn_typed_param_count`), and the v0.17 call-site
// validator fires:
//
//   * MT4055 — row var declared but no fn-typed param can bind it
//             AND the fn has multiple non-fn params
//   * MT4056 — fn has both concrete effects AND a row var with no
//             fn-typed param (the row var is structurally inert)
//   * MT4057 — row var lives on the return side, no fn-typed param
//             (v0.16 active emit)
//   * MT4058 — caller's lambda-arg count doesn't match the callee's
//             fn-typed-param count
//   * MT4059 — caller's closed-row enclosing fn can't accept the
//             effects the closure brings through the row sub
//
// v0.18 ships the matching PARSER SURFACE: `!{| E1, E2}` and
// `!{fs | E1, E2}` now parse, so the multi-row-var fn shape is
// finally writable at the source level (previously the HIR could
// represent it but no parser could produce it). See
// `crates/mty-syntax/src/parser/types.rs::effect_row_tail`.
// A canonical row-poly fn: one row variable, one fn-typed param.
// The closure's effects flow through `E` into the caller's
// inferred effect set at each call site (per RFC-008 §inference).
// (`_` prefix keeps the helper out of the WIT export world — the
// example focus is the SIGNATURE syntax, not exportability; mirrors
// the convention used by 22_effect_row.)
fn _each[E](f: fn() -> Unit) -> Unit !{| E} {
}

// v0.18: a row-poly wrapper that runs two closures in sequence,
// each with its OWN row variable. The caller's inferred effect set
// is the union of all closure rows — `E1` from `a`, `E2` from `b`.
//
// This is the v0.18 motivating shape — pre-v0.18 it had to be
// modelled by chaining two single-row-var calls (the v0.17 typeck
// already handled it via per-call-site RowSubst); now the parser
// accepts the natural form.
fn _cross[E1, E2](a: fn() -> Unit, b: fn() -> Unit) -> Unit !{| E1, E2} {
}

fn main() {
  log("23_multi_row: RFC-008 multi-row-var signature shapes (see _each, _cross)")
}
